1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Retreat! Retreat!

2
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Not a trap!

3
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Presence of humans, so many, did not account for.

4
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Well now, I see you're quick to comprehend languages.

5
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Alright, tell us, who are you exactly? Are you perhaps residents of the Golden City?

6
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:40,000
We are merely interference units. We are made to observe, touch, search, and gather.

7
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:47,000
New language. New outward appearances. We would like to learn more about you. We would like to gain information.

8
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Oh, I get that. There's a ton we want to know as well. So why don't we talk it out, eh? Let's really get to know each other.

9
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:09,000
Eventually, we would come to find out that even if this truly was the Golden City, compared to our homelands that cast us aside, it was a far more harsh environment.

10
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:20,000
The only way back would be using this thing that got us here.

11
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:22,000
But how do we use it though?

12
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Do we even know how to get it up and running again?

13
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:27,000
We have no choice but to try.

14
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:36,000
When we arrived at the Shoto region, the ritual site's altar just started running on its own, and we were able to descend.

15
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:41,000
We discovered it was due to a nearby hollow clutching a special stone.

16
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:45,000
I don't know why he was even there, but...

17
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:49,000
After we put him inside, the altar began to move.

18
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:55,000
It was necessary for us to test whether or not he could make the altar go back up.

19
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:02,000
It worked, and after a few hours, it came back down again.

20
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:04,000
What?

21
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:11,000
But sadly, we learned humans cannot return from this area and still maintain their human form.

22
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:14,000
Listen up, Wazukyan has a report.

23
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:19,000
Okay, everyone, the legendary Golden City does indeed exist.

24
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:22,000
It stretches out before us, untouched.

25
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:25,000
Yet we cannot go beyond it, nor can we return from it.

26
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:28,000
We find ourselves standing within a legend.

27
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:32,000
And we're the only ones who can find the truth of that legend.

28
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:34,000
We've already abandoned our homelands.

29
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:37,000
If we can't leave, we shall make a new beginning here.

30
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:43,000
We shall become the first citizens of the Golden City at the bottom of the world!

31
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:49,000
It is only in this miraculous place that one can achieve their greatest wish.

32
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:52,000
And as we found out...

33
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:58,000
We did not all need to be prophets touched by the Divine to believe these powers to be true.

34
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:06,000
How's it looking?

35
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:09,000
If we cut down on rations, they'll last about seven days.

36
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:12,000
But the water will probably go a bit faster.

37
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:15,000
I'm sure that interference unit knows where to find water.

38
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:19,000
I already asked. Securing the root is the main issue.

39
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:23,000
Since they are not living beings like we are, the curse doesn't affect them.

40
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:28,000
Which of course is the reason why they don't know how much one can ascend without triggering the deforming curse.

41
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:30,000
Well, yeah, that is a problem.

42
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:34,000
What's this? I wish we knew what it says.

43
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:39,000
Soikyu soishi, Metsukorijasu.

44
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:41,000
Oh, wait, you can read it?

45
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:42,000
Mine!

46
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:46,000
Extraordinary. It contains glyph strings unknown to us.

47
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:50,000
I would guess the literacy rate of their settlement must greatly surpass ours by far.

48
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:55,000
In order to comprehend the Golden City, it seems your knowledge will prove indispensable.

49
00:03:55,000 --> 00:04:01,000
Oh, yeah, that's right. She told me what her name is. It's Idomyui. She's smart.

50
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:06,000
Fueko, listen. Gather everyone who can read and write. And the interference units.

51
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:09,000
Alright, Idomyui. We're counting on you.

52
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:14,000
So, Idomyui. Where do you think the residents of this place went?

53
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:17,000
Idomyui don't know, but they are not in village now.

54
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:22,000
My village legends tell stories of people with patterns on their bodies to say what they are.

55
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:24,000
We make homage.

56
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:32,000
When one reaches age in my village, we put patterned ink decorations on body meant to imitate the residents of Golden City.

57
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:37,000
But Idomyui's body cannot bear any child inside of it.

58
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:41,000
As part of shame, ink of sacrifice put on Idomyui.

59
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:45,000
What is this thing? How long has it been in here?

60
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:48,000
What's going on, you guys?

61
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:50,000
Fueko! There's something strange in this helmet!

62
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:52,000
When do you think it got in there?

63
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:54,000
Huh?

64
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:58,000
How adorable!

65
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:02,000
Idomyui! It might be dangerous!

66
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:10,000
Oh, wow. I guess it's super tame.

67
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:15,000
For a creature that lives inside a shell to hide, it sure lacks a sense of larryness.

68
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:28,000
Fueko, we cannot afford to keep that creature.

69
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:34,000
It'll be alright. Even docile creatures have managed to survive. They live here. And so, so can we.

70
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:41,000
If we study its way of life, then we can learn from it. It might just provide some sort of breakthrough to help us secure our survival.

71
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:42,000
Yeah.

72
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:46,000
I say we keep the thing here and observe it. If that's okay.

73
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:48,000
Why not? Besides, it's kinda cute.

74
00:05:48,000 --> 00:06:15,000
I've identified some sources of water. There are five at the same level as us where the chance of being hit with the curse is low. Of those, the two larger bodies of water fall within the territory of dangerous creatures. And well, of the remaining three, one has a fallen iron tower in it, so rust has contaminated the water. And another is so hot even the interference units can't approach it.

75
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:17,000
That only leaves one option then.

76
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:25,000
Yes, but the interference units do not need water. So, it'll be up to us to determine whether or not the water is potable.

77
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:53,000
It looks clear. And it doesn't smell.

78
00:06:53,000 --> 00:07:00,000
No, wait. We have to boil it. For now, let's just bring some back. Everyone's waiting.

79
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:23,000
Now we just need some food. Having a secured source of water, we finally had a foothold. Now we had to make sacrifices along the way. Little by little, we acquired the skills to stay alive in the brutal golden city.

80
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:30,000
What's wrong, Ida Mui? Are you alright?

81
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:37,000
Ida Mui, Ida Mui, I feel a little hot.

82
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:41,000
Ida Mui smells like mommy.

83
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:46,000
What? So is that the reason? Is that why in the beginning you felt attached to me?

84
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:53,000
Mommy's smell. The smell of mating with lots of people. Mommy's very important. So she has lots of children. But Ida Mui only girl child come from mommy. Only one to be born. So big brother's nice to Ida Mui. But when they examine Ida Mui insides, find out no have kids like mommy. They said that Ida Mui is cursed. Cursed one born of giant.

85
00:07:53,000 --> 00:08:00,000
So must go back to giant pit, so must go back to giant pit where cursed one belongs. Mommy and big brother's not like hearing.

86
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:08,000
Ida Mui is cursed. Cursed one born of giant pit, so must go back to giant pit where cursed one belongs.

87
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:29,000
Mommy and big brother's not like hearing. Don't look at Ida Mui anymore after that. They... they said that Ida Mui... not child anymore. They said...

88
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:44,000
Ida Mui, uh, so you know, I can't have kids. And so I'm very sorry, but, uh, I... I can't exactly take the place of your mother.

89
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:54,000
No replacement for mommy. Ida Mui wants wiggles. Ida Mui don't want to be thrown away ever again.

90
00:08:54,000 --> 00:09:09,000
At first, I had wanted to find the light. But in the end, the only thing I finally found waiting for me... was more darkness.

91
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:19,000
But what a... what a very warm darkness it was. Ida Mui, I will never let you go.

92
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:32,000
Ida Mui, Ida Mui...

93
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:34,000
Shhhh!

94
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:36,000
Oh!

95
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:39,000
Ida Mui!

96
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:41,000
Whee!

97
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:03,000
Blacko! Blacko!

98
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:07,000
You gotta get up! Come on!

99
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:09,000
Okay.

100
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:12,000
Ida Mui, wake up. It's morning.

101
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:17,000
Ida Mui?

102
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:23,000
Oh my gosh. Diarrhea?

103
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:29,000
Transparent egg casings? Caterpillars?

104
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:34,000
Weko, we need your help!

105
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:39,000
Everyone... just had a slight fever yesterday.

106
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:42,000
Look, something's really wrong with Aicham.

107
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:46,000
The toes look like lead that's been melted and hardened.

108
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:51,000
It looks like everyone else is getting sick too.

109
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:54,000
I-I'll need water to care for them.

110
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:57,000
Also, I think this might be contagious.

111
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:00,000
Okay, Vueko. They're in your hands now.

112
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:02,000
Understood.

113
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:03,000
We'll be back.

114
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:10,000
The fever won't go down.

115
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:12,000
Vueko!

116
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:14,000
What is it this time?

117
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:23,000
It's the food survey team.

118
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:27,000
Only these three were able to make it back and well...

119
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:29,000
They didn't last very long.

120
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:31,000
Why do they... look like that?

121
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:34,000
Achapoca, I'd like to collect a sample of this rock.

122
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:35,000
Do your thing.

123
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:40,000
It's not a rock.

124
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:42,000
Layers piled atop each other.

125
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:46,000
The corpse of a larger creature melted and solidified.

126
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:50,000
We've been tricking the stuff that caused that to happen.

127
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:52,000
So what do you want to do, Belov?

128
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:55,000
There's no other water for us to take back with us.

129
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:57,000
I know. We'll bring it back.

130
00:11:58,000 --> 00:11:59,000
We do still need the water after all.

131
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:01,000
Though we will need to tell them.

132
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:03,000
Hey, Vueko.

133
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:05,000
This was inside his bag.

134
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:07,000
Any idea what it is?

135
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:12,000
Did our Prophet, touched by the Divine, have some kind of premonition?

136
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:14,000
I think it's some sort of relic.

137
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:16,000
Though I don't know what it's used for.

138
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:17,000
Huh.

139
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:19,000
Think that interference unit might know something?

140
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:25,000
Or did the supernatural power of the Great Pit sense our creation send it to us?

141
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:27,000
Either way, that was it.

142
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:30,000
That was the turning point.

143
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:36,000
The water itself is a living organism.

144
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:41,000
Those things in the feces were probably some kind of eggs or seeds.

145
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:44,000
But we... I mean, we even boiled it!

146
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:48,000
These guys here sure keep surprising us with their creative survival tactics.

147
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:52,000
And now, we no longer have a safe watering hole for us to source.

148
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:58,000
The only options that we're left with are to continue allowing this pseudo-water to ravage us and make us sick.

149
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:01,000
Or to reject it and die of unrelenting thirst.

150
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:07,000
Eating and drinking in this place has always been a challenge. But now we're in a truly tough spot.

151
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:13,000
The onset and symptoms differ from each person. We might find a way to combat it by examining everyone.

152
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:15,000
Times of the essence.

153
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:18,000
Can I just add one thing?

154
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:22,000
Where did you obtain?

155
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:27,000
I believe the food survey team that brought this back went around to all the traps we set.

156
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:30,000
Do you have any idea where they might have come across it?

157
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:32,000
Do not know.

158
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:36,000
Those kids were still alive and in relatively good shape when they first got here.

159
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:39,000
Does this relic perhaps have something to do with all this?

160
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:42,000
Indeed. It is responsible.

161
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:44,000
Round relics are the shape of wishes.

162
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:48,000
Some are modest. Some are strong, like this one.

163
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:51,000
Wait, Wishes? What kind of wish made them like that?

164
00:13:52,000 --> 00:14:01,000
Incorrect. Not just any kind of wish. That is Cradle of Desire. To put it in your way of speaking, it is wish-granting egg.

165
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:08,000
You should not touch directly. If you are consumed, your wish will dissipate.

166
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:16,000
Adult humans are diverse and complex. They are not suited. If you wish to make use of it, a juvenile is best.

167
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:30,000
Not good. They need to drink water. But this water ravages their bodies.

168
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:36,000
It hurts, Wiko. It hurts.

169
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:38,000
It hurts.

170
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:39,000
What's wrong?

171
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:48,000
Your hand. Does it hurt? Turn back to normal, please!

172
00:14:57,000 --> 00:14:59,000
You mean that wish-granting egg?

173
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:03,000
Even if adults can't, it should work for a child to use, won't it?

174
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:12,000
Fear felt by a juvenile is much closer to origin. The probability is very high.

175
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:14,000
Give it a try.

176
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:20,000
We have too many worldly thoughts. Let's bet on that kid's wish.

177
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:23,000
Wazukyan, why isn't Belov here?

178
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:27,000
He's finally fallen ill as well. Trying to be brave.

179
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:29,000
He's sick?

180
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:32,000
We don't have much time left to spare. I'm counting on you, Vueko.

181
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:41,000
Have faith now. I know that kid will be our salvation.

182
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:50,000
We have been forced into disgrace and expelled. We have had our home taken from us, and our descendants.

183
00:15:50,000 --> 00:16:00,000
Irum Yui is the baby sister of those descendants. There is a hand that could save us, but if we do not reach out, we'll once again lose our place to belong.

184
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:03,000
I beg you. Get better.

185
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:07,000
Wazukyan said that he knew the kid would be our salvation.

186
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:13,000
It was the first time I'd seen him close up. The face of a divinely possessed prophet.

187
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:17,000
I feel so, so hungry.

188
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:21,000
Vueko! Vueko!

189
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:23,000
Vueko!

190
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:27,000
Vueko!

191
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:33,000
But you're...

192
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:35,000
Adam Yui, you.

193
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:40,000
Look at me, Vueko. It doesn't hurt at all.

194
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:41,000
Mom!

195
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:48,000
Adam Yui, come this way.

196
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:54,000
Even though she's full of energy, and she says her hand doesn't hurt,

197
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:57,000
obviously something's not quite right.

198
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:00,000
I wonder what the child wishes for to heal like that.

199
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:03,000
The thing is, she doesn't seem to remember.

200
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:07,000
Hey, if you keep messing with it, it'll start hurting.

201
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:08,000
It doesn't hurt!

202
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:10,000
What do you think?

203
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:12,000
Why don't we leave this to Vueko?

204
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:14,000
We'll devote ourselves to acting as support.

205
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:18,000
She has the most earnest emotional bond that any of us with Ida Mui.

206
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:22,000
I'd like to believe that Ida Mui's wish is somehow related to that as well.

207
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:36,000
We were near our breaking point. There were very few of us left. And those who could still walk were dropping day by day. If I were to fall ill as well, Ida Mui would be left here all on her own.

208
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:39,000
Ida Mui, are you awake?

209
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:44,000
Vueko?

210
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:45,000
Ida Mui!

211
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:47,000
Ida Mui!

212
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:50,000
You're changing! How are you feeling today?

213
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:52,000
I'm just fine.

214
00:17:56,000 --> 00:17:58,000
Why Vueko? Why sad looking?

215
00:17:59,000 --> 00:18:05,000
It's nothing. I'm just confused. I have to ask you, Ida Mui. Don't you ever get sad sometimes?

216
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:09,000
You're here Vueko, so it's fine.

217
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:16,000
You know, they say that your body is trying to change into the body you wish you always had, Ida Mui.

218
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:18,000
Huh?

219
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:23,000
All I could do was pray that the choice I made wasn't the wrong one.

220
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:34,000
With this wish-granting egg, did Ida Mui perhaps wish for her own happiness? For her own fears to vanish?

221
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:36,000
Wait a minute for her.

222
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:37,000
Ida mui!

223
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:39,000
lobby to hang two together!

224
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:40,000
For her to hit, bow your head was tired for the encouragement.

225
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:46,000
Where are you?

226
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:47,000
ices?

227
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:49,000
Meagie!

228
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:50,000
Why are you screaming?!

229
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:53,000
Vueko, do you see?

230
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:56,000
A baby?!

231
00:18:57,000 --> 00:19:00,000
I didn't know how to react.

